<title>CHINA: China Legend signs $110 million U.S. export deal.</title>
<headline>China Legend signs $110 million U.S. export deal.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Legend Group has signed a $110 million deal to export 105,000 branded computers to North America over the next two years, the Xinhua news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Legend, which is China's leading personal computer maker and controls the Hong Kong-listed Legend Holdings, signed the deal with US-based Source One Enterprises at a trade fair in the southern city of Guangzhou, the agency said.</p>
<p>It gave no other details of the deal but said it was considered a breakthrough for China's domestic personal computer industry.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
